※ pl4g-test: compile=ok run=native,qemu exit=0
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4217 LANG_TYPE_EXACT_FLOAT_COMPARISON

※ Two floating-point values arrived at by different routes are rarely the one
※ value even where the numbers they stand for are equal, so asking whether
※ they are equal is warned about.  It is a warning and not an error because
※ the question is sometimes the right one -- and `@[ignore(4217)]` is how a
※ program that means it says so, which the test beside this one does.

let a: mut f64 = 1.5f64
let b: mut f64 = 1.5f64

@[visible]
let same: mut bool = false

@[startup, impure]
fn main() → u8:
    same ← a = b
    0u8
